# #688: an ALLOWLIST. The app code is baked into the image, so the build context must never carry
# secrets, data, .git, agent worktrees, backups, tests or anything else a checkout collects. Start by
# excluding everything, then let back in only what the Dockerfile COPYs. A new top-level file or
# directory stays out until it is listed here on purpose. scripts/check_image_layout.py checks this.
*

!Dockerfile
!requirements.txt
!core/
!web/
!mcp_server/
!assets/

# ...and nothing generated or stray inside those.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.bak*
**/*.backup*
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
# The build stamps its own version (Dockerfile ARG CONSTRUCTICON_VERSION); a VERSION.json left in a
# checkout by an older deploy.sh must not ride along and contradict it.
core/VERSION.json
